2026-10-19T22:24:23.1645470Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57212
2026-10-19T22:24:23.1646155Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [FEATURE]: Plugin API: list sessions and child sessions by parent ID
2026-10-19T22:24:23.1649873Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Problem

A plugin cannot list sessions. A plugin cannot list the child sessions of a session. The plugin session API has no list operation.

## Source (v2.0.31)

- `packages/plugin/src/promise/session.ts:153` selects the host operations for plugins:

  `export type SessionDomain = Pick<`

  The selection lists `create`, `get`, `remove`, `switchAgent`, `switchModel`, `prompt`, `generate`, `command`, `compact`, `synthetic`, `interrupt`, `update`, `move`, `wait`, and `context`. It has no `list`.
- `packages/client/src/effect/api/api.ts:124` shows that the host list operation accepts a parent filter:

  `readonly parentID?: Session.ID | null | undefined`

## Purpose

A plugin sends a message to all child sessions of a session. The plugin must know the child session ids. Today the plugin records each child id when it makes the child. The plugin cannot find a child that a different component made.

## Proposed minimal API

Add `list` to the plugin session domain. Give the current `SessionListInput` through. A plugin then calls `ctx.session.list({ parentID })`.

## What the plugin does today without it

The plugin keeps its own map from parent id to child ids. The map is not complete after a restart, and after a different component makes a child.

